  <title>Shaje, your backstage pass | The Struggle Bus</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Your seat is saved. A personal invitation to The Struggle Bus with Vinny O’Brien." />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" /><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Tilt+Neon&family=Archivo:wght@400;600;700;900&family=Space+Mono&family=Yellowtail&family=Permanent+Marker&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/backstage/room.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <header class="studio-header"><a href="/">THE V SPOT <span>STUDIOS</span></a><span class="room-label">DRESSING ROOM 01</span><button id="lights" aria-pressed="true">Lights are on <span aria-hidden="true">◉</span></button></header>
  <main>
    <section class="dressing-room" aria-label="Your personalised dressing room">
      <div class="room-set" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="mirror-copy"><p class="overline">THE STRUGGLE BUS / WITH VINNY O’BRIEN</p><h1><span id="greeting">Shaje,</span><br/>your seat is saved.</h1><p class="handwritten">First your story. Then, a bigger conversation.</p><button class="check-in" id="accept">Count me in <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p class="small-status" id="accept-status">A personal invitation. No keynote required.</p></div>
      <div class="chair-name" aria-label="Your director’s chair"><span id="chair-name">SHAJE</span><small>OUR GUEST</small></div>
      <div class="sticky-notes" aria-label="Open your backstage notes">
        <button class="sticky yellow" data-open="conversation"><span class="note-number">01 / FROM VINNY</span>Your<br/>conversation<span class="note-foot">Read the note ↗</span></button>
        <button class="sticky blue" data-open="booking"><span class="note-number">02 / CALL SHEET</span>Pick your<br/>recording time<span class="note-foot" id="booking-note">Find your slot ↗</span></button>
        <button class="sticky pink" data-open="assets"><span class="note-number">03 / HAIR & MAKEUP</span>Headshot<br/>& a little bio<span class="note-foot" id="assets-note">Your good side ↗</span></button>
        <button class="sticky cream" data-open="audience"><span class="note-number">04 / GOOD COMPANY</span>Who’s<br/>listening?<span class="note-foot">Meet the audience ↗</span></button>
      </div>
      <p class="set-caption">Wine is a prop. Curiosity is compulsory.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="call-sheet"><div><p class="overline">YOUR CALL SHEET</p><h2>We’ll take care<br/>of the production.</h2></div><ol class="progress" aria-label="Your production progress"><li id="step-accepted"><span>01</span> You’re in <small>Awaiting check-in</small></li><li id="step-booked"><span>02</span> Recording booked <small>Pick a time</small></li><li id="step-assets"><span>03</span> Assets received <small>Headshot and bio</small></li><li id="step-ready"><span>04</span> Ready to record <small>We’ll send the recording link</small></li></ol><p id="pilot-notice" class="pilot-notice">Pilot preview. Explore every note. Check-in and uploads become available through the personal pass created in Vinny’s guest room.</p></section>
    <section class="bigger"><div class="bigger-heading"><p class="overline">THE CONVERSATION CAN GO FURTHER</p><h2>Heavy topic.<br/><em>Light on its feet.</em></h2><p>Human agency. AI literacy. The choices we still get to make. Let’s give people a way into the conversation that makes them want to stay.</p></div><div class="format-preview"><button data-open="formats"><strong>60</strong><span>SECONDS IN THE HOT SEAT</span><p>One subject. An expert. A clock with terrible manners.</p><b>Try a question ↗</b></button><button class="scenario" data-open="scenario"><strong>Who gets<br/>to decide?</strong><p>An AI recommendation has a sponsor. Do you still trust it?</p><b>Take your seat ↗</b></button></div><button class="text-link" data-open="collaboration">The bigger idea for 2027 ↗</button></section>
    <section class="guest-voices"><p class="overline">THE COMPANY YOU’LL KEEP</p><blockquote>“Culture beats strategy<br/>a million times.”<cite>Tren’ness Woods-Black / The Struggle Bus</cite></blockquote><p>Previous guests include Paula Macaggi, Matt Ezyk, Bryan House, Harvey Bierman and James Ullman. Different lives. Plenty to talk about.</p><a href="https://open.spotify.com/show/6aWq1IdNxcXJVGiJMLByqO" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Hear the show ↗</a></section>
  </main>
  <footer><span>THE STRUGGLE BUS</span><p>A VSpot Media programme. From Tralee, with curiosity.</p><button data-open="prep">Before we record ↗</button></footer>

  <dialog id="conversation"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">A NOTE FROM VINNY</p><h2><span class="guest-name">Shaje</span>, there’s a seat for you.</h2><p id="personal-brief">Friday’s conversation took us from government and technology to something much more personal: how we keep the ability to think, choose and act for ourselves.</p><p>I’d like to start with you. What shaped you, what changed your thinking, and what makes you keep going when people welcome an idea but nobody acts on it.</p><p>We’ll follow the interesting thread. You don’t need to arrive with a polished success story.</p><p class="handwritten signature">Vinny</p><p class="fine" id="scope">One Struggle Bus episode first. The wider collaboration is a separate conversation.</p></dialog>
  <dialog id="booking"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">YOUR CALL SHEET</p><h2>A time that<br/>works for you.</h2><p>Allow 45–60 minutes. We finish before 6pm Dublin time. The recording is conversational, on StreamYard, with nothing to install.</p><a id="booking-link" class="action" href="https://calendly.com/vinnyob/struggle-bus-recording-1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Choose your recording time ↗</a><p class="fine">Use the email address Vinny invited. Your booking confirmation and calendar invitation come from Calendly.</p><button id="verify-booking" class="secondary">I’ve booked. Check my call sheet.</button><p id="booking-message" role="status"></p></dialog>
  <dialog id="assets"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">HAIR & MAKEUP / MOSTLY METAPHORICAL</p><h2>Your good side.</h2><p>A headshot you like and a short bio, written how you’d want to be introduced.</p><form id="asset-form"><label>Headshot<input name="headshot" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp" /><small>JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 3MB.</small></label><label>Your introduction<textarea name="bio" rows="4" maxlength="1500" placeholder="Two or three lines about you, in your own words."></textarea></label><label>Anything to ask, or keep off limits?<textarea name="notes" rows="3" maxlength="2000" placeholder="Only Vinny and the production team can see these notes."></textarea></label><label class="permission"><input name="permission" type="checkbox" value="yes" required /> I’m happy for this headshot and bio to be used to introduce and promote my appearance.</label><button class="action" type="submit">Send to production ↗</button><p id="asset-message" role="status"></p></form></dialog>
  <dialog id="audience"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">PEOPLE ARE ALREADY LISTENING</p><h2>Good company.<br/>Across the channels.</h2><div class="audience-numbers"><p><strong>5,814</strong>Audio plays & downloads<small>August 2026 / shared Struggle Bus and Nearly News feed</small></p><p><strong>16,950</strong>LinkedIn followers<small>30 September 2026</small></p><p><strong>3,854</strong>Free Substack subscribers<small>August 2026 review</small></p><p><strong>1,520</strong>YouTube subscribers<small>30 September 2026</small></p></div><p class="fine">From the October 2026 partner pack. Audio plays and downloads aren’t unique listeners or a Struggle Bus-only total. Other figures cover Vinny’s wider audience. Audiences overlap and are not added together.</p></dialog>
  <dialog id="formats"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">THE EXPERT HOT SEAT</p><h2>60 seconds.<br/>How hard can it be?</h2><p>A specialist-subject quiz with our own title and rules. We test the facts, then explain the revealing answer. The clock can wait while we do the thinking.</p><p class="sample-question">Does an AI recommendation always mean a product is the best fit?</p><button id="reveal-answer" class="action">Show the answer ↗</button><p id="quiz-answer" hidden>No. Ask which criteria shaped it, including any paid placement. A useful conversation starts with that question.</p><p class="fine">A sample of the proposed format. We’ll agree subjects and review the questions before recording.</p></dialog>
  <dialog id="scenario"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">WHO GETS TO DECIDE?</p><h2>The recommendation<br/>has a sponsor.</h2><p>Your AI assistant picks a product. Then you learn the seller paid for placement. Do you still trust it?</p><div class="choices"><button data-choice="A">A / Yes, if it suits me.</button><button data-choice="B">B / Only if it tells me.</button><button data-choice="C">C / Show me alternatives.</button></div><p id="scenario-response" role="status">Pick a response. Nobody loses their parking space.</p><p class="fine">Your answer stays on this page and isn’t saved. The guest and audience choose, we reveal another fact, and see who changes their mind.</p></dialog>
  <dialog id="collaboration"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">A SEPARATE IDEA FOR 2027</p><h2>A bigger room<br/>for the conversation.</h2><p>A small pilot of expert quizzes, a scenario game and deeper interviews. An A to Z glossary makes the concepts easier to explore. Later, an adult university audience could bring its own questions.</p><p>We want human consequences to become a routine part of ecommerce’s AI conversation: who has control, who benefits and who can challenge a decision.</p><p>Vinny handles production and investigates partners. Shaje brings expertise and potential contributors. We agree scope, funding and shared use of the assets before committing to the wider programme.</p><p class="fine">This is a proposed collaboration. Checking in for the podcast doesn’t accept a commercial agreement.</p></dialog>
  <dialog id="prep"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">BEFORE WE RECORD</p><h2>Come as you are.<br/>Bring headphones.</h2><ul><li>A laptop or desktop with a camera, headphones and a reliable connection.</li><li>A quiet room, with light in front of you rather than behind.</li><li>Your StreamYard link will arrive separately. No software to install.</li><li>Tell Vinny what you’d like to discuss and what’s off limits.</li><li>We aim for a 30–40 minute finished conversation. Jokes get room to breathe.</li></ul></dialog>
  <dialog id="access"><button class="close" aria-label="Close note">×</button><p class="overline">YOUR BACKSTAGE PASS</p><h2>A little privacy.<br/>A warm welcome.</h2><p>Enter the guest password Vinny sent with your invitation. It unlocks your check-in, call sheet and asset submission.</p><form id="access-form"><label>Your guest password<input type="password" id="guest-password" autocomplete="current-password" required maxlength="80" /></label><button class="action">Open my dressing room ↗</button><p id="access-message" role="status"></p></form></dialog>
  <script src="/backstage/room.js" is:inline></script>
</body>
</html>
